# Country prefixes, full sample ISINs, and boundary characters for the checksum gate.
# `XS`/`EU` are structurally valid but ISO 3166-1 unassigned, steering the mutator toward
# inputs where `Isin::country()` returns `None`.
"US"
"GB"
"DE"
"XS"
"EU"
"US0378331005"
"GB0002634946"
"XS0000000009"
"0"
"9"
"X"
